​While investigating the count mismatches between Teradata and Databricks for the digital_dashboard_control table, I discovered one of the root causes. In Teradata, all data sources are queried from a single location. However, in Databricks, our data is split across two different catalogs (for example, EECOL and WIS are sitting in dev_eecol_engineering, while the rest are in our main catalog).
​Because our current notebook only reads from the main catalog, we are completely dropping those sources.
​To fix this and accurately mimic the Teradata output, I am planning to combine the data from both catalogs using a UNION ALL when we build our initial temporary views (sf_sales_fact, of_order_fact, etc.) in the Databricks notebook.
​Does this approach sound good to you? Let me know and I will go ahead and implement the fix.